WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.295
(Latin rumba music)

00:00:05.865 --> 00:00:08.485
- [Voiceover] This is
the Chicken Maharaja.

00:00:08.485 --> 00:00:10.293
I guess it's like their Big Mac.

00:00:10.293 --> 00:00:11.424
Must be.

00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:12.655
- There's a lot of bun here.

00:00:12.655 --> 00:00:14.756
- Oh my god.

00:00:14.756 --> 00:00:16.184
- I don't think this is
the same sauce they use

00:00:16.184 --> 00:00:17.577
in a Big Mac, it can't be.

00:00:17.577 --> 00:00:20.340
- It's chicken, it's not
beef, but what can you do.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.745
- This is amazing.

00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:26.343
This is American opulence
exported to India at its finest.

00:00:26.343 --> 00:00:28.920
Like yeah, let's just put all
of it in there, what the hell.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.300
- It's actually a lot
better than I thought.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.398
- [Voiceover] So here we
have the McAloo Tikki burger,

00:00:35.398 --> 00:00:39.542
aloo is potato, so I'm
assuming it's gonna be

00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:41.481
a lot of potato in here.

00:00:41.481 --> 00:00:44.024
- It's got the McDonald's
quality I've come to learn

00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:44.906
to, uh..

00:00:44.906 --> 00:00:47.240
- Well, it looks like a
burger in the US, kind of.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.581
- It's a little sad looking.

00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:52.144
- Don't know what that tastes like.

00:00:52.144 --> 00:00:53.873
- It's got some good, you know,

00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:56.392
good flavors that I associate with India.

00:00:56.392 --> 00:00:57.971
- What's interesting
about this is that it's

00:00:57.971 --> 00:01:00.491
absolutely no idea what is in this.

00:01:00.491 --> 00:01:02.058
And the inside of the patty is green,

00:01:02.058 --> 00:01:04.542
the sauce is orange, and
it's covered in onion.

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:05.564
Like, you know.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.840
- There's so many vegetarians
in India, obviously,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.527
they have to make some veg product.

00:01:10.527 --> 00:01:14.242
- Fifty cents, that's a good deal.

00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:17.747
- [Voiceover] This is the
big Spicy Chicken Wrap.

00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:19.582
- This is American size. (laughs)

00:01:19.582 --> 00:01:21.405
- It's confusing, how to...

00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:23.286
- I think it's like,

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:25.419
Oh.

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:30.063
- It's actually pretty close
to what it is in the US.

00:01:30.063 --> 00:01:31.642
It's a bit more spicy, but...

00:01:31.642 --> 00:01:34.950
- Again, there's all the
sauces and mayos, it's so much.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.181
- This might actually
be the spiciest thing

00:01:36.181 --> 00:01:37.365
I've ever eaten at McDonald's.

00:01:37.365 --> 00:01:39.362
And it's like this
creeping one that's like

00:01:39.362 --> 00:01:42.554
coming up the back of my mouth.

00:01:42.554 --> 00:01:47.415
- [Voiceover] This is a
100% Paneer Passion McSpicy.

00:01:47.415 --> 00:01:49.120
- I still love that they put the "Mc"

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.561
in front of everything.

00:01:50.561 --> 00:01:52.117
McPaneer, okay.

00:01:52.117 --> 00:01:55.855
- Kinda looks like a
deep-fried French toast.

00:01:55.855 --> 00:01:57.318
- Is this just a giant hashbrown?

00:01:57.318 --> 00:01:59.396
- The cheese, I guess it's a cheese patty?

00:01:59.396 --> 00:02:02.554
- And we've got the McDonalds India token

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:04.510
mysterious orange sauce.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.407
- Oh wow, that's spicy.

00:02:07.407 --> 00:02:09.961
- (coughs) Oh, there's the spice!

00:02:09.961 --> 00:02:12.318
- This is food that you
would just eat in bed

00:02:12.318 --> 00:02:13.734
at like, three in the morning.

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.021
- The paneer's a little
weird, but I guess it's

00:02:16.021 --> 00:02:17.658
kinda like tofu in that way, it just

00:02:17.658 --> 00:02:19.771
takes on the flavor of
whatever's on top of it.

00:02:19.771 --> 00:02:21.756
- This is something I
think could possibly be

00:02:21.756 --> 00:02:23.498
successful in the US.

00:02:23.498 --> 00:02:25.994
- I feel like McDonald's India
was literally put together

00:02:25.994 --> 00:02:28.338
by someone just perusing
a Wikipedia article

00:02:28.338 --> 00:02:31.137
for Indian food, and putting
a "Mc" in front of it.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:35.270
(rumba music)

